WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>Shanghai</b>

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.530
<i>As the embers of world war 
smoldered in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.240
<i>the Imperial Army established</i>

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:17.630
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.890
<i>a clandestine spy training agency.</i>

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.550
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.440
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.030
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.490
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.010
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.110
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.600
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.700
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.400
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.820
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:28.890
Episode 4 - City of Temptation

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.650
<b>Military Police
Kosei Unit</b>

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:52.040
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.020
Sorry. I didn't mean to keep 
you waiting, Sergeant Honma.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.080
Not at all, Captain Oikawa, sir. 
What can I do for you?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.250
I called you here because I have 
a top-secret job for you.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.020
We have an enemy spy within 
the Shanghai Military Police.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.470
I want you to find out who it is.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:08.060
Why me, sir?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.080
I've only been stationed in 
Shanghai for three months.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.430
That's precisely why.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.870
It's been a little over three 
months since the leaks started.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.840
In other words, you can't be the culprit.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.990
Plus, I hear you served in the 
Special Higher Police back in Japan.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.870
The man I'd originally had investigating
this was killed yesterday.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.080
That was MP Corporal Miyata Nobuteru.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.420
Here are Corporal Miyata's reports.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.960
Pardon me.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.060
Sergeant Honma! What are you doing?!

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:51.920
I'm sorry, sir!

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.980
Confirm the location.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.290
The International Settlement.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:08.530
Damn it.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:16.020
That's... my house.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.090
How awful...

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.520
She's the maid who came to my house daily.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.120
What about the rest?

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.880
Do you recognize any of the other bodies?

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.310
Inspector James...

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.040
Let's see...

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.220
I'm fairly sure these two are the beggars

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.020
I often saw sitting in front of my home.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.500
This one, tragically, is a child who lived nearby.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.850
He often played behind the house.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.280
The last one... I have no idea.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:57.790
I see.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.710
Then he's the most suspicious one.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.300
The beggar?

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.380
You're saying he's behind this terrorist bombing?

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.050
He probably had a cookfire going or something.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:14.350
It must've caused the paint can 
sitting by the wall to blow up.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.340
That's absurd!

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:18.530
This was clearly a terrorist making
an attempt on the captain's life!

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:20.000
After yesterday—

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.690
Enough, Sergeant Honma.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:25.980
It's pointless. They never had any intention

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.480
of investigating this incident.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:33.340
Well, that settles that, then.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:34.760
Take care.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:40.230
I left early this morning

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.270
so I could talk to you.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.230
If I'd left at my usual time...

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.740
My schedule may have already been leaked.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.110
I'll leave what we discussed to you.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:52.340
Sir.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.240
What is it, Private Yoshino?

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:15.580
Did you know him?

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:19.520
No, sir. I didn't know him.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.120
Excuse me.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.510
My, it's been a long time since we spoke!

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:52.990
Enforcing Justice 
on Behalf of Heaven

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:49.160
I'm in your debt for 
everything you did for me.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.950
<b>Shanghai Nichi-Nichi News 
Writer
Shiozuka Hajime</b>

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:55.950
Shiozuka Hajime...

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:02.270
Wait, didn't I investigate you 
on charges of operating

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:03.960
a left-wing magazine?

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.930
Yes, about three years ago.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:10.880
I trust you've turned over a new leaf 
and started working a respectable job?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.510
Oh, as respectable as can be.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.250
More respectable than
anything I've done before.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.010
If you think I'm lying, read for yourself.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:26.520
Shanghai Nichi-Nichi 
News - Evening Ed.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:26.520
<b>Mortars destroy south area building 

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:23.210
I wrote this, and there's not 
a single word in it that

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.300
paints the Japanese 
army in an unfavorable—

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.520
The incident from yesterday?

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.770
Yes, it was terrible.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.820
A building that housed a 
Japanese business was hit by

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.680
five mortars and utterly destroyed.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:35.740
I already know about this.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.950
Ah, I see I'm preaching to the choir.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:42.300
And the target of that last bombing 
was Captain Oikawa's home...

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:46.020
The anti-Japanese terrorism 
here is getting quite bad.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.530
But there's no need to get too serious.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.140
This might all be resolved before you know it.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.860
What do you mean?

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:04.740
Actually, while investigating for that article,

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:07.150
I caught sight of someone unexpected.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.330
Kusanagi?

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.500
And who is this Kusanagi?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.500
The ringleader of that left-wing 
magazine I took the fall for.

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.180
We were classmates at the imperial university.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.940
Last month, when I returned to Japan,

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:34.940
another former classmate 
and I went out drinking.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:38.680
He's with the Home Ministry 
Police Affairs Bureau.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.330
Kusanagi?

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.900
Yes. The same Kusanagi you 
used to hang out with.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:50.650
It's just a rumor,

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.380
but I've heard about a Japanese activist

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:55.650
who joined an overseas 
anti-Japan organization.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.780
And supposedly the man
in question is none other

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.620
than Kusanagi Yukihito.

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.560
Let me get this straight.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:06.730
You're saying your old friend from college

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:10.630
has snuck into Shanghai to carry 
out anti-Japan activities?

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:14.590
Well? That's enticing information, isn't it?

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:17.440
And what is this Kusanagi

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:20.680
trying to accomplish here in Shanghai?

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:23.860
Obviously, I have no way of knowing that.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:24.640
However...

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:29.900
It seems Kusanagi made contact 
with the late Corporal Miyata.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.170
What?

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.660
Do you have a picture?

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.490
Now we're talking.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:39.320
Sadly, it's just a class picture 
from our university days.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:42.980
That's Kusanagi.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:45.410
I'll leave that for your reference.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:49.570
Oh, no need to thank me.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:51.410
Just make this give-and-take.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:53.570
Let me know if you uncover any juicy info.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.510
Kusanagi...

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:17.990
<i>Is there a link between 
Corporal Miyata's death,</i>

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:21.710
<i>the bomber's attempt on Captain Oikawa, 
and the intel leaked by the spy?</i>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.920
<i>I have to find him quickly,</i>

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:26.510
<i>or we can forget stopping 
anti-Japan terrorism.</i>

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.680
<i>No one in our unit could trust anyone else,</i>

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:31.180
<i>and the whole group would 
collapse from within.</i>

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.880
<i>But how am I going to find a lead?</i>

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.040
This is...

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.590
A dance hall?

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:14.350
No.

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.740
<i>Can't get in for free, huh?</i>

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:18.950
<i>Oh, well.</i>

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:26.080
<i>What is this? When did...</i>

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:55.920
Thank you.

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:03.880
<i>That's a boy!</i>

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.160
Hey, do you know him?

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:17.050
Oh, yeah, he's a regular.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:20.300
Knows how to make a scene when 
he's playing around. Makes me jealous.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:39.370
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:43.350
You had something to report on the 
truth behind the incident, correct?

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:45.730
Yes, sir, I do.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:50.660
The entire incident in question, 
Captain Oikawa, sir,

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.370
has been a cover-up, 
which you yourself engineered.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.290
What's your rationale?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.750
The day before the bombing,

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.160
there was an attack where a building

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:05.030
<b>Mortars destroy south area building 

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:05.030
Shanghai Nichi-Nichi 
News - Evening Ed.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:02.390
that housed a Japanese business

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:04.730
was destroyed by multiple mortars.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.300
Therefore, it would only be natural

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.800
to anticipate a second or third round.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:12.300
But you, Captain,

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.110
moved straight to the window,

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:15.430
without any hesitation,

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.350
in the moment after the explosion.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.590
Because you knew there 
wouldn't be a second one.

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:25.540
You blew up your own home,

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:28.900
using the frequent anti-Japanese 
terrorist acts in Shanghai as a cover

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.930
in order to conceal your own crimes.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.860
And as a result, multiple innocent people

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:37.000
lost their lives, as well.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.590
Innocent, you say?

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:44.540
You can't possibly be referring 
to that pair of beggars

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.840
who always sat in front of my house, right?

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:51.750
Or maybe you mean the old 
maid who came to my house?

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.330
You're mistaken, then.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.240
That woman was constantly

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:58.140
pilfering little things from me.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:01.860
Where in this city can you 
find anyone who's innocent?

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:05.860
No one anywhere is going 
to care that they're dead.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.320
So, you admit it?

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.610
That you blew up your house?

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:17.620
What if I did?

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:25.390
Your five years here have been too long for you.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:32.610
Here in Kosei, the most chaotic 
district in Shanghai,

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:36.540
with your earnest, fastidious personality,

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:40.200
you dedicated your whole being 
to carrying out your mission perfectly.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:42.940
Until...

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:45.490
You snapped.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.000
Oikawa-san.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:14.540
As always, we truly 
appreciate your patronage.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.590
Actually, I have a proposition for you.

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:21.160
Do you think a bit of the opium in 
your vault that's just sitting there

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:24.260
could make its way to us?

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:27.630
If so, I could introduce you to even more

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.770
enjoyable forms of entertainment.

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.730
But then, someone noticed that the 
amount of opium in the vault

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:40.530
didn't match what was in the record book.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:43.080
Corporal Miyata was never

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.590
trying to uncover a spy.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:50.730
He was pursuing the opium 
missing from the vault.

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:59.940
That bombing was a complete 
farce, which you engineered

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:02.500
in order to hide the body of that young boy.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:08.260
So, what is it you want?

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:11.520
Please admit the truth behind 
Corporal Miyata's death.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:15.730
Obviously, that includes what 
happened to the boy who shot him.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:20.010
If I do that, the best case is I'm dismissed,

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:23.490
and at worst, I'm court-martialed.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.310
You have no choice.

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:29.310
How will you make anyone believe you?

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:31.290
What did you....

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:34.690
You say I set everything up.

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.530
But you have no proof.

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:40.020
All you have are your own words.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:42.640
If you were to die here,

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.640
they'd never see the light of day.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:52.320
If I die, the letter I've 
written containing the truth

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:54.360
will be sent to the Ministry of War!

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:05.620
Fine.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:09.710
I give up. I'll do as you say.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:13.340
You're not going to try and 
commit suicide, are you?

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.220
Suicide?

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:22.820
Never!

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:26.020
What do you think dismissals

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.760
or court-martials <i>are</i>?

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:33.720
Listen. If five years in Shanghai 
have taught me anything,

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.320
it's that no matter what 
crimes people commit,

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:38.690
no matter what kind of 
disgrace they suffer,

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.990
they can survive!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.670
I don't care if I take another life,

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:45.790
or destroy this MP unit.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:47.940
I'll do anything and everything I can

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:50.660
to continue feasting at this banquet!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:52.170
And I'll live,

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.650
live, live, live,

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:57.250
and enjoy every moment until the bitter end!

00:19:57.580 --> 00:20:00.040
The old maid, the beggars, 
and even that kid...

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:02.220
Why should I care how many of them die?!

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:03.780
You know,

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.750
the cheapest commodity in Shanghai

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:08.240
is human life!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:14.860
Huh?

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:17.980
Stop it, Private Yoshino!

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:25.370
Why?! Why did you shoot Captain Oikawa?!

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:30.120
Revenge for my lover.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.410
Lover?!

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.470
Who in the world are you—

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:35.790
You can't mean...

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:43.400
Don't!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.870
<i>I learned two years ago that classified info</i>

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:05.560
<i>was being leaked from the 
Japanese Army in Shanghai.</i>

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:09.470
<i>My investigation led to 
the discovery of a casino</i>

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:12.670
<i>frequented by Shanghai MP Captain Oikawa.</i>

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.390
<i>In addition to opium, he was selling</i>

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:17.590
<i>secret intelligence on the black market.</i>

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:22.940
<i>He planned to accuse a 
fellow MP, Sergeant Honma.</i>

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:26.890
<i>Now, the Military Police will 
mostly be able to save face.</i>

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:29.730
<i>As a result of all this, 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki</i>

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.350
<i>forced the Army to recognize 
what was going on in Shanghai.</i>

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:39.860
<i>I'll probably end up sticking around 
here for a little longer...</i>

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:45.300
<i>In this city of temptation, where betrayal</i>

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:47.230
<i>and solitude intertwine.</i>

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:23.170
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:22.880
You look tired.

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:26.210
I've been incredibly sleepy lately.

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:28.920
Sleep when you're sleepy.

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:34.880
Episode 5 - Robinson

00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:34.880
When the time comes, 
you'll wake up on your own.
